# hyprlock PAM stack — local password check only, no pam_faillock.
#
# Arch's stock file is "auth include login", which chains into system-auth
# and its pam_faillock (compiled defaults, faillock.conf is all comments:
# deny=3, fail_interval=900, unlock_time=600). Three fumbled attempts at
# the lockscreen lock the ACCOUNT: even the correct password is then
# rejected for 10 minutes — at hyprlock, TTY logins and sudo alike.
# 2026-11-02: hit for real.
#
# A lockscreen is not a login surface: it guards a running session. The
# data-at-rest boundary is LUKS; the login path on this machine is the
# tty1 autologin override (see .root/README.md). Brute-force lockout
# policy belongs to sudo/su/TTY, which keep their faillock untouched.
# Tradeoff accepted: the lockscreen itself no longer rate-limits guessing
# — password strength is that boundary.
#
# pam_unix verifies the same local unix password as before. No nullok:
# an empty password never unlocks.

auth            required        pam_unix.so